   "source": [
    "Let's select just the Adelie and Chinstrap penguins."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "df = df[(df['species']=='Adelie')|(df['species']=='Chinstrap')]"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Now we will grab the flipper length and bill length to be the features (stored in ``X``) and the species as the labels (stored in ``y``)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "X = df[['flipper_length_mm','bill_length_mm']].values\n",
    "y = df['species'].map({'Adelie':0,'Chinstrap':1}).values"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Exercises"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "1. Fit a binary linear classifier using scikit-learn (see ``sklearn.linear_model.LogisticRegression``).\n",
    "\n",
    "Plot the resulting classifier using ``plot_decision_regions(X, y, clf=model)``.\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "text/plain": [
       "<Axes: >"
      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 6,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    },
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 640x480 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "model = sklearn.linear_model.LogisticRegression()\n",
    "model.fit(X,y)\n",
    "\n",
    "plot_decision_regions(X, y, clf=model)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "2. Print out the coefficients of the line (``model.coef_``).  Interpret these values (in terms of the direction of the line and also what they tell us about how the classifier operates)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "[[-0.15845623  1.17936568]]\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "print(model.coef_)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "3. Calculate and print out the accuracy of the classifier using the `.score` function.  Interpret this value."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "0.9579439252336449\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "accuracy = model.score(X, y)\n",
    "print(accuracy)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "4. Try different combinations of features and print out the accuracy for each one.  Interpret your results."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "0.9719626168224299\n",
      "0.7383177570093458\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "X2 = df[['bill_length_mm','bill_depth_mm']].values\n",
    "model2 = sklearn.linear_model.LogisticRegression().fit(X2, y)\n",
    "print(model2.score(X2, y))\n",
    "\n",
    "X3 = df[['flipper_length_mm','body_mass_g']].values\n",
    "model3 = sklearn.linear_model.LogisticRegression().fit(X3, y)\n",
    "print(model3.score(X3, y))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "The combination of bill length and bill depth is the best classifier that we tested, with an accuracy of .972"
   ]
  }
